# The Python extension surface.
#
# Kept OUT of the core modules because export pymodule is a stage1-only
# feature: stage0 rejects the keyword, and every core module must compile with
# both compilers. Only build_pymodule.sh compiles this file.
#
# This host surface deliberately grows one source-backed controller at a time.
# The browser's common ABI remains the authority for the complete registry, but
# Python may expose a controller when it has the same lifecycle, source-backed
# state, and display-list ownership rules. Generic preview/configuration/
# session exports remain absent until they have a real implementation.
#
# The runtime source is included because stage1 lowers sview_len/sview_at only
# when the runtime Elisa source is present in the unit. The pymodule build
# links a small shim instead of the prebuilt runtime object.
